      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CATS QUARTERS (7) gets the nod despite recent form that reads modestly, because the shape of the assignment is much kinder than her latest Class 1 sixth at Taree. She drops into BM50 grade, gets weight relief, has wet-track experience and profiles better at 1600m than her sprint run two back suggests. CLASS REVOLUTION (3) is the clear danger if his Wauchope second is taken with the excuses attached; he was the well-supported favourite, blundered and was held up, though this is tougher. DUPONT (5) is in the mix after finishing fourth in a provincial Class 4 at Gold Coast when unwanted in the market, and the easier company gives that run more weight. DANCING TILDA (4) is harder to recommend on two recent soft-track defeats, but the quick back-up, class drop and previous win at this track and distance keep him in calculations if he finds his earlier local form. RAISED BY WOLVES (6) has yet to miss the placings here. Include.",
